From e2db80ca07c390d31a676ab7d8a60135f5d918cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:03:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] power: supply: bq256xx: Enable charging at probe

The driver programs the charge voltage and current limits at probe but
never the charge enable bit (CHG_CONFIG), assuming the reset default.
Motorola's bootloader on the moto g82 5G (SGM41542) leaves it cleared,
so the phone never charged under Linux. Set it in hw_init, after the
watchdog and before the limits.

Also read CHARGER_CONTROL_0 from the chip rather than the register
cache: it holds CHG_CONFIG and the self-clearing watchdog reset, and a
cached copy that disagreed with the chip turned a charge_type write into
a no-op.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
index 945b85c2f..60541ad3d 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -1272,6 +1272,7 @@ static bool bq256xx_is_volatile_reg(struct device *dev, unsigned int reg)
 {
 	switch (reg) {
 	case BQ256XX_INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT:
+	case BQ256XX_CHARGER_CONTROL_0:
 	case BQ256XX_CHARGER_STATUS_0...BQ256XX_CHARGER_STATUS_2:
 		return true;
 	default:
@@ -1614,6 +1615,16 @@ static int bq256xx_hw_init(struct bq256xx_device *bq)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Charging is enabled at reset, but a bootloader may have turned it
+	 * off; the limits programmed below are what keep it safe.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(bq->regmap, BQ256XX_CHARGER_CONTROL_0,
+				 BQ256XX_CHG_CONFIG_MASK,
+				 BQ256XX_CHG_CONFIG_MASK);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = power_supply_get_battery_info(bq->charger, &bat_info);
 	if (ret == -ENOMEM)
 		return ret;
